# chained cross-lib — the ROOT
library "Root".

// Composes over `"Sib"."Sib Chained"`, a foreign boolean comp that has its OWN cross-lib operand. Per Option-(a)
// (disc 465 §1) the index projects "Sib Chained" NON-total (conservative), so the root LOUD-fails `operand-not-
// total` — even though Sib really emits "Sib Chained" total. This is the documented conservative-loud behavior:
// never a silent wrong emit; the topological Option-(b) projection is deferred.

concept "Root Records":
- type is Observation.
- shape is RecordSet.
- code is `root-rec`.

concept "Root Flag":
- value type is boolean.
- defined as exists ( "Root Records" ).

concept "Cross Chained":
- value type is boolean.
- defined as ( "Sib"."Sib Chained" and "Root Flag" ).

activity "Refer":
- request CPGServiceRequest.

decision "Triage":
- when "Cross Chained" then recommend activity "Refer".
